=== PARITY ===
Ported web/src/api/hooks/useCommands.ts (2 reads, 0 mutations) -> UI-free KMP state holder
CommandsStore over the S7 CommandsRepository. Endpoints/params verified against the web hook's
template literals and internal/api/router.go (the per-vehicle `/commands/history` + `/commands/latest`
GET routes at router.go L2900-2901). The web hooks apply only `select: (data) => data ?? []` (a
presentation null-guard) and no client-side derivation, so the rows round-trip verbatim.

Reads (2) -- cache-then-network StateFlow<Resource<JsonElement>>:
 1. useCommandHistory -> store.commandHistory(vehicleId)   GET /vehicles/{vehicleId}/commands/history?limit=200
        cached under commandHistoryKey ('history:{id}') = web commandKeys.history(id)
        ['command-history', id]; staleTime QUICK (10s); fixed `limit=200` carried verbatim.
        enabled: !!vehicleId -> a null/blank id returns the stable disabled feed that never
        fetches and stays at the initial Loading slot (asserted: no upstream collection).
 2. useCommandLatest  -> store.commandLatest(vehicleId)    GET /vehicles/{vehicleId}/commands/latest
        cached under commandLatestKey ('latest:{id}')  = web commandKeys.latest(id)
        ['command-latest', id]; staleTime MODERATE (15s); no query parameters.
        enabled: !!vehicleId -> same disabled-feed gate as above (distinct instance per read).

Mutations (0): the web hook file contains only two useQuery's and no useMutation, so there is no
invalidation surface -- the holder exposes refreshCommandHistory / refreshCommandLatest (the
cache-then-network re-collect; a no-op for a null/blank id or a feed nobody observes).

Cache: CacheDomain.Commands (10s freshness window). The two web staleTimes (history QUICK 10s,
latest MODERATE 15s) collapse onto the domain window; the finer refetch cadence is a UI/S8 concern
(mirroring how the web staleTime only gates the freshness flag, not whether the refresh runs). Both
reads share the single Commands partition under the distinct prefixed keys above so each
(vehicle, feed) caches independently while logout clears the whole domain in one call.

SI preserved: command audit rows carry id / vehicle_id / command / params / status / error /
created_at -- ids, strings, and timestamps, not unit-bearing -- so they are carried as raw
JsonElement and round-trip through the cache unchanged; conversion is display-only (S5). The
contract test additionally asserts no imperial suffix (`_mph`/`_kwh`) ever appears in the cached
payload.

Derivations: none (web hook only `select: data ?? []`) -> no golden vectors required, matching the
Anomalies precedent (a non-derived JsonElement passthrough domain). KMP + Windows C# parity is
therefore carried entirely by the verbatim endpoint/param/key contract above; there is no per-value
logic that could drift between platforms (ADR-004).

